r55 predictions reproduced: 16/16  (mismatches=0)
shapes disagree on 7/16 cases

-- the two relations are incomparable (witnesses on identical bytes) --
  A 'g2g4 e2e4'      r45-shape=False  r55-real=True
  B 'g2g4\nnope\n'   r45-shape=True   r55-real=False

-- normalization surface --
  r55 split(): splits on any of 29 Unicode whitespace code points (incl. U+00A0, U+3000); r45 split('\n'): only U+000A (after universal-newline translation)
  r55 case folding: none (str.upper never applied); digit-width folding: none (U+FF12 != '2'); unicode normalization: none (raw str equality)
  r45 newline handling: read_text() universal newlines, so lone \r also separates lines
  r45 tokenization is LINE-based (split('\n')); r55 tokenization is TOKEN-based (split())

-- multiplicity --
  r55 compares sorted LISTS: a duplicate adds an element -> equality breaks
  r45 membership ignores multiplicity entirely: the same line 1000 times still passes
